{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons","id":802411,"title":"Removing the Gears in Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-06T16:09:42-08:00","id":802411,"title":"Removing the Gears in Demons","content":"It's been said by a few people that they dislike the technological nature of Demons and the God-Machine (though I personally disagree, liking how well it fits with Ezekiel). Now, I understand the preference of Demons should be more mystical rather than bio-mechanical beings, as it is a valid preference. But what I don't understand is why the technological nature is hard to remove? <br /> <br /> Can the issue be fixed in your personal games by simply restricting access to Demonic Form abilities that are technological? If not, what other things conflict with altering the to your desire? As far as I'm aware, everything else in the game is fitting for more generalized interpretations of demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T16:34:55-08:00","id":802434,"title":"","content":"Most of the sample form descriptions have the first being a technological monstrosity and the other being more hellfire and brimstone themed ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T16:46:25-08:00","id":802445,"title":"","content":"We could probably catalog the simple reskinning needed to remove the &quot;machine&quot; interpretation.<br /> <br /> I mean, even Data Form can be recast. Anyone else read the part in <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=1&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiZ2rC4u5bKAhVL5SYKHXkDCh0QFggdMAA&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FGood_Omens&amp;usg=AFQjCNE_RHfHfQ6EXVLmFeE1XUAWprD8nA&amp;sig2=s5FaFRVweaKSg1Vc_LR9Qg\" target=\"_blank\">Good Omens</a> with moving via the telephone lines?<br /> <br /> &quot;Then again, you might just as well ask how many demons can dance on the head of a pin.&quot; ... &quot; But if you look from really close up, the only problem about dancing on the head of a pin is all those big gaps between electrons.&quot;<br /> <br /> So there's even precedent for <i>that</i>.<br /> <hr /><br /> Heck. Open challenge:<br /> <br /> Ask for non-&quot;cyber&quot; interpretations (of up to 4 things at once) in Demon that are &quot;too mechanical&quot;, and I'd bet I or someone else can re-skin it in a more &quot;classical/spiritual/whatever&quot; manner, no rules changes needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-06-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T15:43:51-08:00","id":803393,"title":"","content":"Here's some rationales I've written down. Lemme know if it works, or I'm full of sh*t. ^_^;<br /> <br /> \u2022 Embeds are infallible cosmic truths that demons can enforce onto themselves. Exploits are akin to manipulating the &quot;legalese&quot; of reality, albeit temporary.<br /> \u2022 Terms like propulsion, infrastructure, etc. are simply used to dumb down advanced ideas for &quot;primitive mortals&quot; to comprehend.<br /> \u2022 The God-Machine is not just a collection of machinery, cogs, and gears, but the Spirit of Order itself. Every time a pattern is formed, the God-Machine knows, because they are one in the same.<br /> \u2022 GM is to Demiurge as Promethean Principle is to God(?), perhaps polar opposites, or parent to the other (or both).<br /> \u2022 The demonic form isn't truly made of mundane materials. Rather, a demon is a collection of symbolic truths bound in a quantum state between one or more realities (wow that's a mouthful)--uh, it is a True Name given physical form?<br /> \u2022 The Cipher is a Malapraxis?<br /> <br /> But yeah, I didn't mean Spirit as in Shadow, as more like the GM is sentient symbolism. Software and Hardware are too temporal to equate to something so powerful. The Idea behind the GM, that is what transcends the mundane. It doesn't need circuit boards, not in the conventional sense. Patterns that act akin to circuits, such as leylines touching menhirs to connect with other realms, that is what forms the GM. Transcendental, not material. Ignore the literal idea of a Machine and think bigger, more abstract. It's not a mere robot, but patterns within patterns, made sentient by means unknowable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 01-07-2016, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T17:58:26-08:00","id":803456,"title":"","content":"I don't really get why people have a problem with the technological horror demons are. I personally love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:04:00-08:00","id":803460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803456#post803456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really get why people have a problem with the technological horror demons are. I personally love it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen. Demon: the Fallen still exists if you want classic demons, and is doubly accessible with the Translation Guide now. Inferno is still out there. In Nomine is still a fantastic game, if you want to try that out.<br /> <br /> Demon: the Descent is different and weird, just like how Promethean and Changeling and Mummy are all unique tweaks on their base monsters. Let it be what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:06:50-08:00","id":803464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803393#post803393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't need circuit boards, not in the conventional sense. Patterns that act akin to circuits, such as leylines touching menhirs to connect with other realms, that is what forms the GM. Transcendental, not material. Ignore the literal idea of a Machine and think bigger, more abstract. It's not a mere robot, but patterns within patterns, made sentient by means unknowable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's kinda what It <i>is</i>, mostly (the material thing being the only major difference I see - to me, It is strongly grounded in the material). The G-M is the sum of its many patterns, not a big computer, and the menhirs and ley-lines thing is basically canon. It just uses what appears to be advanced technology as well (and freely integrates the two) because it works in the material world and isn't omnipotent. It can do incredible things, but It has to do the legwork. The resources are there to build circuitboards (and sometimes they're just efficient, especially in modern times) and fundamentally, to It, there really is no difference between a magical circuit made of ley-lines and a magical circuit made out of metal and silicon. All they are are means to an end, whatever that may be. You can play up this side and downplay the gears easily enough, though crucially It's still a Machine even without cogs and wiring (thinking about it, as written the God-Machine is a vast, sentient occult Rube-Goldberg machine rather than Deep Thought).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:08:02-08:00","id":803466,"title":"","content":"But the name &quot;Demon&quot; is misleading. You're not a demon, you're a machine dressed up in demonic trappings. It sets wrong expectations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:15:57-08:00","id":803470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803466#post803466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the name &quot;Demon&quot; is misleading. You're not a demon, you're a machine dressed up in demonic trappings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're a programmed being created without free will who discovered it. You're a rebel against a Demiurge that created you and, while not all powerful, is damned close. Also you can trade in souls. Demon is an appropriate term. The same description applies to a traditional demon, arguably even down to the programmed part, just most Descent demons go for a sci-fi look (but this isn't mandatory, of course). You can say 'They're machines, not fallen angels!' but it's no less wrong to say 'Well, aren't fallen angels effectively malfunctioning machines?'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:18:46-08:00","id":803472,"title":"","content":"So what, if the Splat was Vampires instead of Demons, you'd be fine with them replacing the classic depiction of Kindred with robots? Yeah, I guess you have cWoD if you wanna play normal vampires. World of Darkness is about creating conspiracies out of the classical depictions of monsters. This looks more like something out of Eclipse Phase than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:30:51-08:00","id":803479,"title":"","content":"Then what attracts you to <b>Demon the Descent</b> rather than <b>Demon the Fallen</b>?<br /> <br /> Different rules? Well there's a Translation Guide; I'm not sure what the writers could do more to cater to you. All you have to do is see Horns and Claws as Demonic Forms and Hellfire as an Exploit - all in the <i>core book</i> - to know your 'typical' depictions are indeed represented. So what else is it you wanted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T18:34:13-08:00","id":803481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803479#post803479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then what attracts you to <b>Demon the Descent</b> rather than <b>Demon the Fallen</b>?<br /> <br /> Different rules? Well there's a Translation Guide; I'm not sure what the writers could do more to cater to you. All you have to do is see Horns and Claws as Demonic Forms and Hellfire as an Exploit - all in the <i>core book</i> - to know your 'typical' depictions are indeed represented. So what else is it you wanted?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know how hard it is to convert all that into more occultic-themed jargon? Not to mention getting other players to stop calling it by the original term (which ends up confusing the hell out of everyone, pun not intended)? You're asking the ST to white-out a LOT of terminology, and then slapping his/her wrist when they complain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T19:35:58-08:00","id":803506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803466#post803466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the name &quot;Demon&quot; is misleading. You're not a demon, you're a machine dressed up in demonic trappings. It sets wrong expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Done this song and dance before.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://nicolelorenz.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/Simpsons-walk-in-walk-out-whistling.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T19:39:14-08:00","id":803508,"title":"","content":"Demon: the Descent is not the game you want it to be, MrParaduo. It's not going to be anything other than what it is, and the very things you dislike about it are why a large number of people here enjoy it. All this thread is going to do is devolve into a messy flame war, the likes of which we've had too many fucking times on this forum already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T20:27:52-08:00","id":803535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803481#post803481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how hard it is to convert all that into more occultic-themed jargon? Not to mention getting other players to stop calling it by the original term (which ends up confusing the hell out of everyone, pun not intended)? You're asking the ST to white-out a LOT of terminology, and then slapping his/her wrist when they complain.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of something I just said in a <b>Promethean</b> thread, too: the games are designed to be modular so that you can rework them to your tastes. What no one seems to realize is that that actually means you have to do some work in preparing your game. It means that the game <i>as published</i> isn't what you were looking for, but the writers have to publish something, right? There's got to be a baseline foundation for a modder to work from. Does it suck? Sure, I guess, but like I said that's why they made the Translation Guide. They met you half way and now it's your turn to do the other half.<br /> <br /> Honestly, 'converting' jargon from one theme to another is probably the <i>easiest</i> fix you'd even have to worry about. Google or Wikipedia some religious terms or use the Seventh Sanctum website's &quot;theo-tech&quot; generator to come up with the &quot;Exodus Mainframe&quot; instead of &quot;Command Infrastructure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally, if your players don't care to switch terms because they don't mind the mechanical aesthetics or can't agree on what theme to play with then you shouldn't be running it for them, right? Just play another game. Sorry if you really wanted to play <b>Demon the <i>Descent</i></b> but there's other demonic games out there. Like I said already, I'm not sure what's left that attracts you to this line at all then.<br /> <br /> I wasn't sold on <b>Demon</b> when it first came out either. I hated it, although I love bio-mechanical imagery in other works. Once I realized it really is a game about demons - as in <i>fallen angels</i> - I warmed up to it. It's still not my favorite game but now I get it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T04:06:07-08:00","id":803652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803393#post803393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's some rationales I've written down. Lemme know if it works, or I'm full of sh*t. ^_^;<br /> <br /> \u2022 Embeds are infallible cosmic truths that demons can enforce onto themselves. Exploits are akin to manipulating the &quot;legalese&quot; of reality, albeit temporary.<br /> \u2022 Terms like propulsion, infrastructure, etc. are simply used to dumb down advanced ideas for &quot;primitive mortals&quot; to comprehend.<br /> \u2022 The God-Machine is not just a collection of machinery, cogs, and gears, but the Spirit of Order itself. Every time a pattern is formed, the God-Machine knows, because they are one in the same.<br /> \u2022 GM is to Demiurge as Promethean Principle is to God(?), perhaps polar opposites, or parent to the other (or both).<br /> \u2022 The demonic form isn't truly made of mundane materials. Rather, a demon is a collection of symbolic truths bound in a quantum state between one or more realities (wow that's a mouthful)--uh, it is a True Name given physical form?<br /> \u2022 The Cipher is a Malapraxis?<br /> <br /> But yeah, I didn't mean Spirit as in Shadow, as more like the GM is sentient symbolism. Software and Hardware are too temporal to equate to something so powerful. The Idea behind the GM, that is what transcends the mundane. It doesn't need circuit boards, not in the conventional sense. Patterns that act akin to circuits, such as leylines touching menhirs to connect with other realms, that is what forms the GM. Transcendental, not material. Ignore the literal idea of a Machine and think bigger, more abstract. It's not a mere robot, but patterns within patterns, made sentient by means unknowable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So what's the issue?<br /> <br /> Note: I'm not seeing how the Cypher is at all related to Malapraxis, personally. More of a True Name, I'd think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803481#post803481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how hard it is to convert all that into more occultic-themed jargon? Not to mention getting other players to stop calling it by the original term (which ends up confusing the hell out of everyone, pun not intended)? You're asking the ST to white-out a LOT of terminology, and then slapping his/her wrist when they complain.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just refluffing and renaming. Why are the players using the old terms? Convenience? That's more on them, then D:tD.<br /> <br /> Is it a lot of work? It's really just replacing words. The mechanics behind the game, the stories you can tell with it, remain unchanged. That seems like were the most headache would go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-08-2016, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T07:39:21-08:00","id":803736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803466#post803466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the name &quot;Demon&quot; is misleading. You're not a demon, you're a machine dressed up in demonic trappings. It sets wrong expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The primary point of this thread is so I can understand why it is a &quot;a machine dressed up in demonic trappings.&quot; rather than &quot;Demons, given a technological coat of paint&quot; to some people. What aspects thematically do individuals who prefer a non-technological nature do you feel is missing in the current game?<br /> <br /> Also, not sure what the issue with embed, infrastructure or cipher are. Embed is using the tricks embedded in reality, infrastructure is the term used for things where you do various projects to lead up to other projects so that you can create an output you desire, cipher just means a mystery to be solved which is what it is mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-08-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T07:55:19-08:00","id":803743,"title":"","content":"With all the usual trappings of demons readily available elsewhere, Descent was always a breath of fresh air to me- not least because of how much I loved the original GM stuff back in core.<br /> <br /> There's the translation guide and homebrew and headcanon options aplenty for you, but OP aren't ever going to do that legwork. It would be a crime if they did. <br /> <br /> Demon is beautiful and tells so many traditional stories in a new way that enlivens tired old tropes. Someone said that the language in Demon robs your wonder, but for me it only ever added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T07:59:49-08:00","id":803746,"title":"","content":"Can people stop mentioning the translation guide in this thread? The purpose isn't &quot;how do I play Demon the Fallen in CofD?&quot;, it's &quot;what elements are an issue for groups and individuals who dislike the technological aspects of Demon the Descent when they homebrew and reflavour things?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:42:24-08:00","id":803768,"title":"","content":"I think some people get too hung up on the technological <u>aesthetic</u>, and ignore the deeper themes. As stated, you can change the aesthetic easily. I'm wondering if there is really anything deeper than that. What about Descent prevents people from telling the Demon (as in Fallen Angels) stories they wish?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T08:43:09-08:00","id":803769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803746#post803746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can people stop mentioning the translation guide in this thread? The purpose isn't &amp;quot;how do I play Demon the Fallen in CofD?&amp;quot;, it's &amp;quot;what elements are an issue for groups and individuals who dislike the technological aspects of Demon the Descent when they homebrew and reflavour things?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want Demon: the Descent without the technological elements, you don't want Demon: the Descent. It's a Gnostic technothriller at it's very core.<br /> <br /> The reason the Translation Guide always comes up is because Demon: the Fallen is the game about classic fallen angels. Demon: the Descent isn't, and it's not so at such a level that trying to change it might be tougher than just scratch-building a new game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T09:58:08-08:00","id":803816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803769#post803769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason the Translation Guide always comes up is because Demon: the Fallen is the game about classic fallen angels. Demon: the Descent isn't, and it's not so at such a level that trying to change it might be tougher than just scratch-building a new game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, I don't really understand how it doesn't work for biblical style angels if you simply remove the technological aesthetic, I'm not sure what themes are missing that posts like this implies. I mean, even if you retain the technological aesthetic to demons, it can still be biblical because of things like the Wheels from Ezekiel. What makes the game unable to represent &quot;normal&quot; angels and demons?<br /> <br /> Restrict access to technological demonic modifications + change name of God Machine to God. What else is really required?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:01:41-08:00","id":803818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803816#post803816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, I don't really understand how it doesn't work for biblical style angels if you simply remove the technological aesthetic, I'm not sure what themes are missing that posts like this implies. I mean, even if you retain the technological aesthetic to demons, it can still be biblical because of things like the Wheels from Ezekiel. What makes the game unable to represent &quot;normal&quot; angels and demons?<br /> <br /> Restrict access to technological demonic modifications + change name of God Machine to God. What else is really required?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing: this game is about angels vs demons with a diesel- and cyberpunk aesthetic (with explicit room for alternate aesthetics based on the time-period and setting). Some people think the aesthetic ruins the mystique. I think that it makes the setting more than just another angels vs demons setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T10:38:55-08:00","id":803839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803535#post803535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reminds me of something I just said in a <b>Promethean</b> thread, too: the games are designed to be modular so that you can rework them to your tastes. What no one seems to realize is that that actually means you have to do some work in preparing your game. It means that the game <i>as published</i> isn't what you were looking for, but the writers have to publish something, right? There's got to be a baseline foundation for a modder to work from. Does it suck? Sure, I guess, but like I said that's why they made the Translation Guide. They met you half way and now it's your turn to do the other half.<br /> <br /> Honestly, 'converting' jargon from one theme to another is probably the <i>easiest</i> fix you'd even have to worry about. Google or Wikipedia some religious terms or use the Seventh Sanctum website's &quot;theo-tech&quot; generator to come up with the &quot;Exodus Mainframe&quot; instead of &quot;Command Infrastructure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally, if your players don't care to switch terms because they don't mind the mechanical aesthetics or can't agree on what theme to play with then you shouldn't be running it for them, right? Just play another game. Sorry if you really wanted to play <b>Demon the <i>Descent</i></b> but there's other demonic games out there. Like I said already, I'm not sure what's left that attracts you to this line at all then.<br /> <br /> I wasn't sold on <b>Demon</b> when it first came out either. I hated it, although I love bio-mechanical imagery in other works. Once I realized it really is a game about demons - as in <i>fallen angels</i> - I warmed up to it. It's still not my favorite game but now I get it</div> </div> </div> </div>Or he could just, y'know, buy the effin' <b>Translation Guide</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T11:21:33-08:00","id":803866,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's be fair here: You <i>can</i> reskin Descent without needing the DTG. The biggest problem comes to what Satchel mentioned, the fact that demons use the language they do to hide from the enemy.<br /> <br /> The technological, scientific, and natural law element of Descent's particular strain of techgnosticism encourages to people think of God and heaven in terms that have always been used by people who tie religion and progress together, particularly Christianity, and that includes a lot of sci-fi (One would be surprised, in fact, at how frequently science fiction-like writings and musings have been offered by religious leaders), but Descent doesn't need to rely on the extremes. Consider that technogaianism allows some bending back, creating the pastoral scenery with technological backings. You can bend the subject back or advance it forward enough that the imagery becomes the wholly organic/spiritual iconography they are all used to-Descent already allows for this, see Horse Barn Infrastructure, or hell, even growing a tree to be infrastructure(Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil cough).<br /> <br /> Descent has always had the capability to be discussed in non-futurism inclined terminology-this is one of the big problems with saying Descent is <i>not</i> about demons. The emphasis on more familiar sci-fi trappings allows the line to be distinct in ways other games on similar subjects can't be, but demons can refer to Facilities as Temples and still be right. Descent, very technically, does not need to use modern terms to describe itself. It does so, not only for the sake of distinction or for spy association, but because it wants to reinforce the strangest notion religious and spiritual icons throughout the ages have always had-describe their 'heavens' as a utopia that can not only be reached, but made.<br /> <br /> When the future has always been divine, it makes sense for the divine to look futuristic. But it doesn't <i>have</i> to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-08-2016, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T11:35:00-08:00","id":803879,"title":"","content":"Holy shit Arc, that was awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[