he DTG. The biggest problem comes to what Satchel mentioned, the fact that demons use the language they do to hide from the enemy.<br /> <br /> The technological, scientific, and natural law element of Descent's particular strain of techgnosticism encourages to people think of God and heaven in terms that have always been used by people who tie religion and progress together, particularly Christianity, and that includes a lot of sci-fi (One would be surprised, in fact, at how frequently science fiction-like writings and musings have been offered by religious leaders), but Descent doesn't need to rely on the extremes. Consider that technogaianism allows some bending back, creating the pastoral scenery with technological backings. You can bend the subject back or advance it forward enough that the imagery becomes the wholly organic/spiritual iconography they are all used to-Descent already allows for this, see Horse Barn Infrastructure, or hell, even growing a tree to be infrastructure(Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil cough).<br /> <br /> Descent has always had the capability to be discussed in non-futurism inclined terminology-this is one of the big problems with saying Descent is <i>not</i> about demons. The emphasis on more familiar sci-fi trappings allows the line to be distinct in ways other games on similar subjects can't be, but demons can refer to Facilities as Temples and still be right. Descent, very technically, does not need to use modern terms to describe itself. It does so, not only for the sake of distinction or for spy association, but because it wants to reinforce the strangest notion religious and spiritual icons throughout the ages have always had-describe their 'heavens' as a utopia that can not only be reached, but made.<br /> <br /> When the future has always been divine, it makes sense for the divine to look futuristic. But it doesn't <i>have</i> to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T13:49:29-08:00","id":805455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803456#post803456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really get why people have a problem with the technological horror demons are. I personally love it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've recently mentioned I want more the the &quot;Religious&quot; type Demons in the next supplement, this is *not* because I dislike the technological horror, it's more because I'd like to know how to convey the religious aspect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the name &quot;Demon&quot; is misleading. You're not a demon, you're a machine dressed up in demonic trappings. It sets wrong expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I repeatedly wish they had called it Daemon, because in computer software a Daemon is a persistent process that runs in the background.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T16:08:13-08:00","id":805565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=805455#post805455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've recently mentioned I want more the the &quot;Religious&quot; type Demons in the next supplement, this is *not* because I dislike the technological horror, it's more because I'd like to know how to convey the religious aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I'm talking about. What religious aspects do you feel are lacking as current in the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T19:20:28-08:00","id":805703,"title":"","content":"well, I started talking about this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement\">here</a>.I suspect neither the GM, nor Demon's really see this as a religious war (though maybe it is, but not in the sense people would think). I find that the books currently tend to briefly mention so religious iconography and then move on. Where I think it lacks is that things are largely said from a Demonic or Angelic perspective, but the real religious aspect is from human perspective. They haven't really explained to us how to build that up, what it looks like. I think if we had more of an idea what the cults look like, the religious undertones might simply fall in place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T20:40:35-08:00","id":805748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=805703#post805703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, I started talking about this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement\">here</a>.I suspect neither the GM, nor Demon's really see this as a religious war (though maybe it is, but not in the sense people would think). I find that the books currently tend to briefly mention so religious iconography and then move on. Where I think it lacks is that things are largely said from a Demonic or Angelic perspective, but the real religious aspect is from human perspective. They haven't really explained to us how to build that up, what it looks like. I think if we had more of an idea what the cults look like, the religious undertones might simply fall in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well they'd probably seem evil because they &quot;take bits of your soul out of your life, they rewrite all of existence at a whim, fight against God and his Angels, they fight against the side that keep the world functioning, they steal peoples lives, they look like horrific demons, they lie to everyone constantly, the fact that they murder random people (who may or may not actually be covers for angels), everyone knows that demons will try to suck you into a pact by giving you things like wealth and status and then screw you over... so most probably wouldn't trust pacts, they terrorize towns based on conspiracy theories, manipulate mortals to get themselves in power, they might destroy your life just so they can get away from an angel&quot; I mean, hell, Demons sounded pretty criminal when I was reading the section on Agencies in the Demon the Descent book.<br /> <br /> As for why they'd look Big and Red with horns. Why wouldn't they? Demons can look like a friggin pillar of fire, they don't need to look cybernetic at all, they can look completely generic demon without issue.<br /> <br /> When it comes to seeing it as a religious war, I'd suggest you give another read to the Agenda's. It is very much a matter of belief and views on what their place is in the world. I mean, one is based around &quot;I don't understand how the world works and am trying to comprehend the ineffable complexity that is reality and God.&quot;, another is the rebels who are on a crusade against God because of their anger or desire for freedom despite the fact that God is what keeps the world turning, another believes that God is truly god and regrets having fallen and is searching for a path of redemption in the eyes of their lord, and the last agenda is focused towards &quot;I am a powerful force who can manipulate reality with ease, am I not a god myself?&quot; <br /> <br /> The cults are light in detail, mainly because they would be ridiculously varied. The cults function like any other cult in real life, except that these ones actually have a divine ephemeral being inspiring it that they can see doing miracles. Ephemeral beings that can mystically bestow you with a mission, turn wood to gold, has eyes of lightning, can grow buildings overnight, can make you feel pure bliss, and can bestow relics to it's followers. In return, you honour it by following it's tenants and do rituals to it in manners like building things in it's name or shunning certain acts as evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-10-2016, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T02:45:20-08:00","id":805930,"title":"","content":"I think that people get too hung up on the whole 'cyberpunk' vibe of Descent (because that's the unexpected bit) and ignore the less computer-ey bits of it. Look at when a demon Goes Loud. They get access to all embeds they have affinity with, they get <i>all</i> exploits, they have a constantly refilling Aether pool. They are practically gods in their own right. Making the God-Machine and the demons themselves more 'gnostic' than 'tech' is just a matter of re-skinning.<br /> <br /> I personally love the idea of the God-Machine being effectively a self-replicating mystical pattern. It's not malevolent, or even sentient as mortals and demons understand it, but it acts and reacts. Like a construct from Conway's Game of Life, but on a cosmic scale. Demons are basically little parts of the pattern that have detached themselves from the whole. If you go by that rationale, anything can be a part of its workings. The rotation of the Earth, the solar wind, the orbits of asteroids, all the way down to the spin of electrons and the movements of quarks. The God-Machine is not <i>in </i>reality, it <i>i</i><i>s </i>reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-04-2018, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:20:08-08:00","id":805946,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, honestly it's a very tricky question to me. I felt like the technology was always more than a superficial surface element to Demon: The Descent, it seemed subtly woven into a lot of design choices within the game. I just can't picture Demon: The Descent without the God Machine elements. <br /> <br /> I'm not trying to be deliberately contrary here, but I do think that some of Onyx Path and White Wolf's other forms of Demons fit the traditional Aesthetic much better. I really liked what they did with Inferno and I thought it was a perfect way of getting across your traditional &quot;The Exorcist&quot; type demons in the World of Darkness. <br /> <br /> I'll keep thinking about this question though and see if I have any ideas about how I'd get it across. (Although personally I like it the way it is, but I understand it's not everyone's cup of tea).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T04:36:36-08:00","id":805978,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean to get rid of the Machine. I meant making it less Machine and more God","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:06:25-08:00","id":805990,"title":"","content":"Also, that means that demonic forms can be less married to the whole biomechanical idea. You could have demon (or angel) whose form is made of living transcendent geometry or endless repeating fractals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:35:21-08:00","id":806002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=805990#post805990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have demon (or angel) whose form is made of living transcendent geometry or endless repeating fractals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, that actually sounds more god-machine than not :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T05:54:17-08:00","id":806013,"title":"","content":"Maybe a True name given physical manifestation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:52:54-08:00","id":806039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=806013#post806013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a True name given physical manifestation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or as close an approximation as can be had in this reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T09:17:25-08:00","id":806145,"title":"","content":"What I meant was that both the God-Machine and the Demons are effectively living patterns. The God Machine is basically a demon on a cosmic scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T09:17:55-08:00","id":806146,"title":"","content":"I like the True Name idea though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T11:49:00-08:00","id":807181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=805455#post805455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I repeatedly wish they had called it Daemon, because in computer software a Daemon is a persistent process that runs in the background.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Deamon in computer software is called that as a reference to Maxwell's Daemon (which itself is referencing the Greek word Daemon), which referred to spirits that enacted various natural processes. The Hebrew word Mal'ak (which translates to Angel) was translated to Greek as Daemon in the Greek version of the Hebrew Bible and that's what the New Testament ended up using for some of the creatures described, others used 'angelos' (Greek for messenger), thus giving us Angels and Demons. The spellings simply changed over the years in English.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T13:16:52-08:00","id":807249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=807181#post807181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deamon in computer software is called that as a reference to Maxwell's Daemon (which itself is referencing the Greek word Daemon), which referred to spirits that enacted various natural processes. The Hebrew word Mal'ak (which translates to Angel) was translated to Greek as Daemon in the Greek version of the Hebrew Bible and that's what the New Testament ended up using for some of the creatures described, others used 'angelos' (Greek for messenger), thus giving us Angels and Demons. The spellings simply changed over the years in English.</div> </div> </div> </div>In sum, <i>Traduttore, traditore</i> is traditional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:08:46-08:00","id":807507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=807181#post807181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deamon in computer software is called that as a reference to Maxwell's Daemon (which itself is referencing the Greek word Daemon), which referred to spirits that enacted various natural processes. The Hebrew word Mal'ak (which translates to Angel) was translated to Greek as Daemon in the Greek version of the Hebrew Bible and that's what the New Testament ended up using for some of the creatures described, others used 'angelos' (Greek for messenger), thus giving us Angels and Demons. The spellings simply changed over the years in English.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> cool history, I still feel like it would have been more fitting, perhaps even more so if it goes from Angel to Daemon. This is one of those &quot;ain't gonna happen things&quot;. I just keep thinking it would be fitting because of the software reference, and to distinguish from other &quot;Demon&quot;s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T20:19:13-08:00","id":807551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=805703#post805703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, I started talking about this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/805258-what-do-you-want-out-of-the-next-demon-supplement\">here</a>.I suspect neither the GM, nor Demon's really see this as a religious war (though maybe it is, but not in the sense people would think). I find that the books currently tend to briefly mention so religious iconography and then move on. Where I think it lacks is that things are largely said from a Demonic or Angelic perspective, but the real religious aspect is from human perspective. They haven't really explained to us how to build that up, what it looks like. I think if we had more of an idea what the cults look like, the religious undertones might simply fall in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; what we've got is an espionage war between the God-Mahine and the Unchained. What we <i>don't</i> have is any sort of indication that either side is in any way concerned with issues such as ethics and morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T21:04:44-08:00","id":807579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=807551#post807551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; what we've got is an espionage war between the God-Mahine and the Unchained. What we <i>don't</i> have is any sort of indication that either side is in any way concerned with issues such as ethics and morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... A lot of Saboteurs and Integrators might argue against that....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T21:10:09-08:00","id":807585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=807579#post807579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... A lot of Saboteurs and Integrators might argue against that....</div> </div> </div> </div>Lot of them wouldn't either.<br /> <br /> It's like Demon's a grey game.<br /> <br /> Eh, you see what I did there? because the game is color coded? Yeah? ...yeah, okay, I'll, um, I'll just, go find a corner and....sit-there-for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T21:23:39-08:00","id":807591,"title":"","content":"also not sure that religion has anything to do with morality or ethics. Dogma however...<br /> <br /> really I think a lot of it comes down to imagery most of the imagery is techgnostic cyberpunk, or completely hidden, very little is described in a religious sense, the cults aren't much described at all. There is no great iron cathedral. No definitive mention of a cog being warn around the neck (cog forhead tattoo's not withstanding). Or perhaps that the cross might actually have another meaning. Do the followers sing hymms? what do they pray? how do they pray? is there a holy book? what is the dogma? How would you stereotype a god machine cultist? how would you stereotype a demon cultist? what do the demon's teach? doesn't leading a cult in a way that presume's your supernatural lead to compromise? Angel's have functions, but nothing describes what function does a giant red horned beast serve (doesn't seem efficient)? basically a lot of demonic forms in the classic sense don't make sense to me. do they, angels, ever actually look angelic or is that just the numina that people see (actually I suspect this is answered and I've forgotten)?<br /> <br /> also to comment what was said previous regarding &quot;like real world cults&quot; I have no real experience with these, and since it's been mentioned &quot;except receiving benefits of the supernatural&quot;... well that's a massive difference. See in the real world there's no proof for any of it. Most people go for community and a feeling of belonging. Also seems like a lot more cults in ChroD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T23:06:14-08:00","id":807638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=807585#post807585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lot of them wouldn't either.<br /> <br /> It's like Demon's a grey game.<br /> <br /> Eh, you see what I did there? because the game is color coded? Yeah? ...yeah, okay, I'll, um, I'll just, go find a corner and....sit-there-for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why I said a lot rather than all or most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the cults aren't much described at all. </div> </div> </div>Because they are too wide-spread and varied. I mean, any information you get on one cult only really represents that one cult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no great iron cathedral. </div> </div> </div>Yet the God-Machine does order it's cults and followers to build structures and temples in it's name all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No definitive mention of a cog being warn around the neck (cog forhead tattoo's not withstanding). </div> </div> </div>Not really sure why that is necessary. Especially since most likely have no idea that there is a technological link between their deity and technology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do the followers sing hymms? </div> </div> </div>Some likely do, some likely don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what do they pray? how do they pray? </div> </div> </div>Each cult likely has it's own unique method of prayer and unique prayers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is there a holy book? </div> </div> </div>Many likely have some holy scipture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what is the dogma? </div> </div> </div>Unique to each cult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would you stereotype a god machine cultist? </div> </div> </div>To do so would be foolish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> how would you stereotype a demon cultist? </div> </div> </div>To do so would be foolish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what do the demon's teach? </div> </div> </div>Depends on that individuals desires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> doesn't leading a cult in a way that presume's your supernatural lead to compromise? </div> </div> </div>Depends on your Cover. I'd assume they would lead to compromise in most covers, but many wouldn't. Also, it is possible to lead the cult in your Demon form or have one of your covers as the prophet of your demon form. Also, there are embeds that would allow you to do it without risking compromise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Angel's have functions, but nothing describes what function does a giant red horned beast serve (doesn't seem efficient)? </div> </div> </div>Well considering Huge Size and Demonic Horns are both Demonic Form abilities that are in the game... and say why an angel would have them... that's.... blatantly wrong?<br /> <br /> But either way, if I wanted to make a generic demon type demonic form at character creation.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Modifications</b></b><br /> Claws and Fangs<br /> Huge Size<br /> Inhuman Strength<br /> <br /> <b>Technologies</b><br /> Demonic Horns<br /> Fire Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Propulsion</b><br /> Wings<br /> <br /> <b>Process</b><br /> Rain of Fire<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> basically a lot of demonic forms in the classic sense don't make sense to me. </div> </div> </div>Read the actual entries for the demonic form abilities, each says reasons why angels might be given them and are given appearances for both classical version and technological version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> do they, angels, ever actually look angelic or is that just the numina that people see (actually I suspect this is answered and I've forgotten)? </div> </div> </div>Throughout the books I believe seen examples of biblical style angels, though more ezekiel style biblical angels than any other (those are the types of angels like multi-headed abominations and the wheels within wheels covered in eyes that the Psychopomp Incarnation is based on).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-13-2016, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T11:38:45-08:00","id":808088,"title":"","content":"As an example of a 'Classic' looking Demon, one of my players Angel was, as far as he knew, charged with guarding Purgatory (it was actually a Facility that did terrible things to Ghosts); as far as he knew, the God-Machine was the Catholic God. As he fell, it warped his Demonic Form to look like that style of demon to match his worldview.<br /> <br /> Another character's demonic form was a six-legged, three-eyed wolf with two poisonous tentacles coming out of his back; that fits more of a more generic demon look, one that would fit well in an anime for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T01:53:19-08:00","id":808523,"title":"","content":"Hi, I'm one of the people that doesn't &quot;get&quot; the technopunk aesthetic. I remember reading the GM story back in the WoD core when it came out and going like &quot;what on earth is this?&quot;. When I finished reading it, I assumed the GM story had been something an author had written and had put so much effort into it that the editor had felt sorry for them and threw it in somewhere random for some quirky weird flavour. I did not &quot;get&quot; the God Machine back then and I certainly don't get it now.<br /> <br /> From a setting standpoint, I'm not comfortable with <i>anybody</i> pulling strings on a global level. It's why I downscale Hunter's conspiracies and other global-scale organisations. I much prefer it when the &quot;ceiling&quot; for powermongering is on a regional level. So the God Machine's core concept just doesn't work for me, even ignoring the mechanistic aesthetics.<br /> <br /> And then Demon. See, my problem is that I didn't like Demon: The Fallen. It was too mired in Abrahamic religion. And now Demon: The Descent misses the mark for me as well.<br /> <br /> Inferno was what came closest to what I wanted, but instead of giving us the tools to play demons (like the two Demon games), it gave us tools for demonic possession, pacts, corruption and suchlike. The reason I liked Inferno was because it hit the closest to how I want demons represented in my games: As incarnations of vice, desires and base impulses. Whenever I've used demons in my games, I've mostly played them as more human-savvy spirits, Ephemeral Entities with Essence and Ranks, who want to grow in power by empowering and guiding mortals into fostering whatever abstract thing they're aligned with.<br /> <br /> Therefore, a Demon game, to me, would be based on what happens when such a creature gains sufficient Rank to break free from the plane they originally come from (whichever it may be) and instead adopt a physical form in the material realm? What if they become &quot;contaminated&quot; by human exposure and start to develop foreign concepts such as empathy, affection and the like? That's the Demon game I want to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T05:55:36-08:00","id":808605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808523#post808523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Therefore, a Demon game, to me, would be based on what happens when such a creature gains sufficient Rank to break free from the plane they originally come from (whichever it may be) and instead adopt a physical form in the material realm? What if they become &amp;quot;contaminated&amp;quot; by human exposure and start to develop foreign concepts such as empathy, affection and the like? That's the Demon game I want to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Narratively, that's the same kind of game that Descent is: an ephemeral creature gains enough power to break free from its base state and adopts a physical form. Angels can fall for a number of reasons beyond just &quot;I became powerful enough&quot;, and there's a built-in antagonist and direction for a game. Dealing with these new-fangled hormonal emotions and human relationships and frailties is a big part of any Unchained's arc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:07:19-08:00","id":808654,"title":"","content":"&quot;I don't like [Thing], what I'd rather see is [exact description of Thing]&quot; is an unusually common sentiment on these boards for some bizarre reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:39:46-08:00","id":808684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808523#post808523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Therefore, a Demon game, to me, would be based on what happens when such a creature gains sufficient Rank to break free from the plane they originally come from (whichever it may be) and instead adopt a physical form in the material realm? What if they become &quot;contaminated&quot; by human exposure and start to develop foreign concepts such as empathy, affection and the like? That's the Demon game I want to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. This sounds very similar to the idea I was working on for a different Demon game (based off of Princess the Hopeful's rules). Basic assumption was Inferno-like demons, made PC-able via co-opting human bodies (much like Demon the Fallen). The Claiming essentially breaks the demon from their fairly 2 Dimensional Sin/Vice focus, and gives them a sense of identity (as well as human context and a degree of empathy). Didn't get very far beyond notes and some recontextualizing details. I could share what I have via PM if you want (and if I can find where the doc is).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808654#post808654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I don't like [Thing], what I'd rather see is [exact description of Thing]&quot; is an unusually common sentiment on these boards for some bizarre reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. There really is no way to satisfy everyone's particular wants and preconceptions. Personally, I find it entertaining to take what one <i>does</i> like, and start fiddling with the mechanics, theme, or fluff to get want you want. Reinvent as little as possible, but shape to taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-14-2016, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:51:43-08:00","id":808783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808605#post808605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Narratively, that's the same kind of game that Descent is: an ephemeral creature gains enough power to break free from its base state and adopts a physical form. Angels can fall for a number of reasons beyond just &amp;quot;I became powerful enough&amp;quot;, and there's a built-in antagonist and direction for a game. Dealing with these new-fangled hormonal emotions and human relationships and frailties is a big part of any Unchained's arc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, first and foremost, the God Machine or equivalent. Not a fan of global puppeteers. Then, the whole &quot;fallen Angel&quot; thing. To me, angels and demons are completely different and unrelated. I also don't think the paranoid espionage angle is fitting or even terribly original. IMO Changeling does it better.<br /> <br /> So beyond the basic core of a demon being a materialised ephemeral entity, there's not much in common at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808684#post808684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. This sounds very similar to the idea I was working on for a different Demon game (based off of Princess the Hopeful's rules). Basic assumption was Inferno-like demons, made PC-able via co-opting human bodies (much like Demon the Fallen). The Claiming essentially breaks the demon from their fairly 2 Dimensional Sin/Vice focus, and gives them a sense of identity (as well as human context and a degree of empathy). Didn't get very far beyond notes and some recontextualizing details. I could share what I have via PM if you want (and if I can find where the doc is).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see it, thank you! I don't particularly enjoy the Claiming aspect (it's either too Geist-y or too much &quot;assuming direct control&quot;), but it could be an alternative, or even the game's antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:56:55-08:00","id":808789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808783#post808783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me, angels and demons are completely different and unrelated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, literally every piece of lore on the subject ever is somewhat against you there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:01:06-08:00","id":808792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808789#post808789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alas, literally every piece of lore on the subject ever is somewhat against you there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can't have it both ways. Either I'm asking for exactly what the game already does, or I'm asking for something genuinely different and original that neither DtF nor DtD can provide. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:06:36-08:00","id":808799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808783#post808783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is, first and foremost, the God Machine or equivalent. Not a fan of global puppeteers. Then, the whole &quot;fallen Angel&quot; thing. To me, angels and demons are completely different and unrelated. I also don't think the paranoid espionage angle is fitting or even terribly original. IMO Changeling does it better.<br /> <br /> So beyond the basic core of a demon being a materialised ephemeral entity, there's not much in common at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The background, antagonist(s), and aesthetic is different, but the narrative arc is <i>exactly</i> the same: alien creature tied to humanity changes to a form to better interact with humanity which comes with new internal conflicts and issues that they must deal with. In your hypothetical game, what would the relationship be between demons who haven't materialized and become &quot;human&quot; be and the PCs? Would they be different creatures at this point? In much the same was as angels and demons in Descent? Would the proto-demons feel betrayed by their material cousins? Would that relationship be worth exploring at all?<br /> <br /> Not to mention, the &quot;angel&quot; and &quot;demon&quot; labels in Descent aren't as commonly used as &quot;Loyalist&quot; and &quot;Unchained&quot; or &quot;Rogue.&quot; It sounds like you're mostly complaining about the language being used.<br /> <br /> All I was trying to say is that you can tell the exact same stories, plus some because of the common antagonist. If that's the problem, you can easily extract it. Though I personally wouldn't find a game that's chiefly about existential musing and pretending to be human terribly interesting. I mean, I guess you could increase the number of demons, give them structured political ideologies, make demons their own worst enemies...<br /> <br /> I dunno. You say you want a game that's exactly like Demon: The Descent, you're just not happy with the aesthetic and background. The superficial elements. That's how I'm reading you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:14:14-08:00","id":808803,"title":"","content":"The thing about the God Machine is that it <i>needs</i> to be global. Otherwise there would be nothing stopping demons from just going where it has no influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:15:20-08:00","id":808804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808799#post808799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno. You say you want a game that's exactly like Demon: The Descent, you're just not happy with the aesthetic and background. The superficial elements. That's how I'm reading you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would bet you actual money that if I made a thread about refluffing the mechanistic aesthetics and getting rid of the God Machine, angels, espionage and technognostic themes, I would be told that I do not actually want to play DtD, that I am removing core, intrinsic parts of the game, and that I might as well just create my own fan splat instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:20:38-08:00","id":808808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808804#post808804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would bet you actual money that if I made a thread about refluffing the mechanistic aesthetics and getting rid of the God Machine, angels, espionage and technognostic themes, I would be told that I do not actually want to play DtD, that I am removing core, intrinsic parts of the game, and that I might as well just create my own fan splat instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. I'd probably disagree with those people. I created a Messenger Integrator once whose entire schtick was that she was originally supposed to tempt and coerce humans into performing certain behaviors, and recruiting potential cultists. Her character arc, defined through her Aspirations, was all about wrestling with her human impulses and urges. Since her background came from influencing relationships, she was greatly conflicted about how the Pacts that she made affected the web of relationships that were already there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:26:22-08:00","id":808811,"title":"","content":"I guess the problem is that you want to play a game about demons as they are in DtD, while stripping out all the reasons that they're like that. So it somehow feels exactly the same and totally different at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:38:18-08:00","id":808825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808804#post808804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would bet you actual money that if I made a thread about refluffing the mechanistic aesthetics and getting rid of the God Machine, angels, espionage and technognostic themes, I would be told that I do not actually want to play DtD, that I am removing core, intrinsic parts of the game, and that I might as well just create my own fan splat instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would be removing core, intrinsic parts of the game with the espionage and angels. Angels are a core feature of the lore that Descent draws from, and espionage is central to the gameplay theme and direction.<br /> <br /> You can reskin the entire game without needing the machinery and techgnosticism-the game already allows for that(But I've had that rant already on page 2). The game is still steeped in the religious and spiritual, it's just subtler than the aesthetic.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest though, you're steadily becoming one of those people I wonder why you're even into the Chronicles of Darkness. Still, so long as you're having fun, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:42:01-08:00","id":808829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=807551#post807551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; what we've got is an espionage war between the God-Mahine and the Unchained. What we <i>don't</i> have is any sort of indication that either side is in any way concerned with issues such as ethics and morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely interesting, and probably the first critique of Demon not being suitable for a &quot;traditional&quot; angels vs. demons game I've read that I can actually understand and agree with. The God-Machine has secret cults of followers, but it's not a genuine religion followed by ordinary people worldwide. Demons are not the amoral opposition to the God-Machine's dogmatic view of morality. I can see how the focus on secrecy and espionage over religion and faith could take the Demon out of Demon the Descent for some people. And unlike the technological aesthetics, that's something you can't easily remove from Descent without changing the game on a fundamental level. And it's something I hadn't even considered because it's such a given to me that any heaven vs. hell conflict in the Chronicles of Darkness would be a secret war between factions that are definitively not the Judeo-Christian versions of heaven and hell. The secrecy is what makes it a CofD game, to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-14-2016, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:52:44-08:00","id":808839,"title":"","content":"There is a sort of ethical divide, in that God tends to lean towards tyrannical order while the demons lean towards anarchy and freedom.<br /> <br /> Still, actually compelling point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:57:07-08:00","id":808848,"title":"","content":"I think it's something to do with the general &quot;Humans know fuck all about how the metaphysics of this world actually work&quot; line. A religion being anywhere close to the truth would be a blow to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:58:19-08:00","id":808850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808825#post808825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest though, you're steadily becoming one of those people I wonder why you're even into the Chronicles of Darkness. Still, so long as you're having fun, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanics. I really like the storyteller system and the only mechanics I've disliked so far has been mage's spellcasting. Every other gameline has had mechanics that are at least acceptable.<br /> <br /> In general, I don't like CofD's grimdark flavour, it generally strikes me as uncritically self-indulgent (Beast in particular is the epitome of this). Once in a blue moon, though there's a gameline whose flavour I actually enjoy, if I excise specific bits (like Changeling and Promethean).<br /> <br /> But mostly it's the mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:05:03-08:00","id":808861,"title":"","content":"Wow. The Chronicles of Darkness are Dark. Who'd have guessed form such a jovial title?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:37:24-08:00","id":808891,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say it's really &quot;grimdark&quot; in the way that the original WoD was; dark, sure, mysterious absolutely, but the only one I can think of that really has an unavoidably grim end is Mummy and that's intentional because it's a Cosmic Horror Story.<br /> <br /> Horror is supposed to make you think, if it's done well. The best horror is morally grey, and maybe a little cynical, in my opinion. But there is hope in the CofD. Many Unchained fall for a connection to humanity, Changelings are perhaps the most hopeful of all the Major Templates, Promethean actually says some great stuff about humanity. These are horror games, but they aren't devoid of light, hope, and the ability to do good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:40:48-08:00","id":808894,"title":"","content":"Is it weird how god damn hopeful and optimistic I actually find the ChroD to be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:44:13-08:00","id":808898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808894#post808894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it weird how god damn hopeful and optimistic I actually find the ChroD to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I'm with you on that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:44:48-08:00","id":808899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808894#post808894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it weird how god damn hopeful and optimistic I actually find the ChroD to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>CofD strikes me as <i>mature</i> in a way that (most of) WoD isn't. It's more about dealing with weird impulses and living in a world of uncertainty and not just surviving but <i>thriving</i>, even when it's easier to be a bad person (or monster, in most cases). Like, all of the games are about striking some sort of balance, whether that's literally what you're trying to do with Werewolf Harmony, or managing your Hunger in Beast, or handling living a secret life in...well all of 'em, really, but specifically Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:46:52-08:00","id":808902,"title":"","content":"Don't let any WoD fans hear you say that, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In all seriousness though, that's something I hope the 4th editions can bring to the WoD. It's a product of the 90s and I think a fresh take would do the game wonders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-14-2016, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:48:33-08:00","id":808903,"title":"","content":"Hey, some of WoD focuses on that. Wraith and Changeling for instance. Changeling is <i>super</i> mature, in that it's literally about balancing being an adult with being a kid. I just also think it's more about getting really angry about the environment and pretending to be a magic mobster. More escapist than CofD, is all I'm saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:50:31-08:00","id":808906,"title":"","content":"In regards to Demon, I find it extremely heartwarming that so many of the Unchained are content with simple ways to achieve Hell. The demon in the opening of the STG is happy to build a housing development and live with a wife and child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:51:42-08:00","id":808908,"title":"","content":"Changeling the Dreaming is such a beautiful game. Lost may be my love, but Dreaming waits patiently to steal me away, and I do not shy away from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:54:31-08:00","id":808911,"title":"","content":"I like how Descent treats trust and faith in others as sacred. Contrary to misconception, the Unchained can trust, and when they find someone or something to trust in, it's a beautiful, precious thing worth fighting for. From identity to lovers and children to even beliefs, Descent's approach to faith feels true to life and powerful.<br /> <br /> Screw fighting the God-machine, I live for that moment when someone holds out their hand and a demon tentatively reaches out to take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-14-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:59:34-08:00","id":808914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808891#post808891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings are perhaps the most hopeful of all the Major Templates, Promethean actually says some great stuff about humanity. These are horror games, but they aren't devoid of light, hope, and the ability to do good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I actually really like the fluff in those games. I mean, I don't hate CofD or WoD, otherwise I wouldn't play it. The world of the CofD appeals to me because it has inherent conflict and potential. It's the perfect setting for people who want to make the world a better place.<br /> <br /> You could say I view the CofD as a renovator might view a dilapidated mansion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:32:58-08:00","id":808950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808911#post808911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like how Descent treats trust and faith in others as sacred. Contrary to misconception, the Unchained can trust, and when they find someone or something to trust in, it's a beautiful, precious thing worth fighting for. From identity to lovers and children to even beliefs, Descent's approach to faith feels true to life and powerful.<br /> <br /> Screw fighting the God-machine, I live for that moment when someone holds out their hand and a demon tentatively reaches out to take it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think my favourite Hell, even though I'm a strong advocate of 'If you wanna go big or even kill/fix the God-Machine in your games, do it', is actually an Integrator reuniting with the God-Machine after completing a self-imposed personal mission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:23:51-08:00","id":809019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808783#post808783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see it, thank you! I don't particularly enjoy the Claiming aspect (it's either too Geist-y or too much &quot;assuming direct control&quot;), but it could be an alternative, or even the game's antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>PM pending.<br /> <br /> As for the Claiming (or whatever), it is kind of necessitated by convention. <b>All</b> of the game-lines have Protagonists that can pass for human, and are modeled on baseline humans. Given a spirit of Sin/Vice, what other justification can you think of for them adopting human appearances and modes of thought (because they have to be relateable, too). They're distinct from Sin-Eaters in that the demon is in control (by virtue of devouring the former tenant's soul).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808803#post808803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about the God Machine is that it <i>needs</i> to be global. Otherwise there would be nothing stopping demons from just going where it has no influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, doesn't Core state that the God-Machine is, in fact, <i>not</i> everywhere? It is just hard for the Unchained without Aether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:29:23-08:00","id":809030,"title":"","content":"It is very present, but it is not omni-present. There are places where God is barely there or even absent. Just kind of far and in-between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:37:08-08:00","id":809038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=809019#post809019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, doesn't Core state that the God-Machine is, in fact, <i>not</i> everywhere? It is just hard for the Unchained without Aether.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons without the God-Machine would be unable to gain Aether on their own but they can in fact still function by using demon-bloods ability to draw in Aether from the Atmosphere. It would probably just get <i>really</i> squicky when the demon finds out that his kids just ran out of their stores of aether, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":885,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","user":"bwgustaf","date":". 01-14-2016, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:46:22-08:00","id":809048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=809038#post809038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons without the God-Machine would be unable to gain Aether on their own but they can in fact still function by using demon-bloods ability to draw in Aether from the Atmosphere. It would probably just get <i>really</i> squicky when the demon finds out that his kids just ran out of their stores of aether, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Everyone always forgets you get Aether, free, if you switch into your demonic form. Granted, that's a compromise roll, but in an area with little-to-no God-Machine presence this is less of an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:51:02-08:00","id":809051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=809048#post809048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Everyone always forgets you get Aether, free, if you switch into your demonic form. Granted, that's a compromise roll, but in an area with little-to-no God-Machine presence this is less of an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>They &quot;forget&quot; because the demonic form is an aggregator, not a generator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T14:18:34-08:00","id":809080,"title":"","content":"You regain lost Aether in Demonic Form, you don't gain new Aether. Going Loud is, in my opinion at least, the &quot;drawing the God-Machine's attention&quot; option. It doesn't help much, if at all, if there is no God-Machine to take notice, especially in the Hedge, since the brief look i took indicates that the demon might actually get themselves in more trouble if they drop cover there in a changeling crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:30:53-08:00","id":809155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=809080#post809080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You regain lost Aether in Demonic Form, you don't gain new Aether. Going Loud is, in my opinion at least, the &quot;drawing the God-Machine's attention&quot; option. It doesn't help much, if at all, if there is no God-Machine to take notice, especially in the Hedge, since the brief look i took indicates that the demon might actually get themselves in more trouble if they drop cover there in a changeling crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: The Descent, page 195</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the demon shifts into her demonic form, she is more attuned to the Aether around her. She can draw in the little bits of processes and mechanisms floating about within the air to fuel her without much conscious effort. The Unchained gains a number of Aether equal to her Primum on her initial transformation into demonic form. <b>Because she is so attuned to the Aether, she can never truly run out of it. Whenever her Aether is reduced to zero, the player can roll Primum, and each success gains the demon one Aether (minimum 1, even if the roll fails)</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. You could perhaps rule that in a 'dead-zone' there's no Aether to draw in (your call as an ST - I avoided making an official ruling on this for the Exclusion Zone or for 15th Century Istanbul). And note this is assuming demonic form, not Going Loud. It's a compromise roll, which is nasty, but if you <i>really </i>need the Aether it's not a dealbreaker. The Hedge is a special case.<br /> <br /> In a world without the God-Machine I'd agree that Aether would be more scarse - perhaps the 'atmospheric' Aether would be gone. The God-Machine will leave considerable remains, though. The Infrastructure won't all disappear, even if a lot of it starts breaking down/malfunctioning/attaining sentience. Surviving demons will presumably start to take over what's left and fight one another for choice territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:23:30-08:00","id":809186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=809155#post809155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Emphasis mine. You could perhaps rule that in a 'dead-zone' there's no Aether to draw in (your call as an ST - I avoided making an official ruling on this for the Exclusion Zone or for 15th Century Istanbul). And note this is assuming demonic form, not Going Loud. It's a compromise roll, which is nasty, but if you <i>really </i>need the Aether it's not a dealbreaker. The Hedge is a special case.<br /> <br /> In a world without the God-Machine I'd agree that Aether would be more scarse - perhaps the 'atmospheric' Aether would be gone. The God-Machine will leave considerable remains, though. The Infrastructure won't all disappear, even if a lot of it starts breaking down/malfunctioning/attaining sentience. Surviving demons will presumably start to take over what's left and fight one another for choice territory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I tend to wobble between narrative and tone when i do read the rules. My interpretations tend to lean towards &quot;will this create good drama&quot; or &quot;will the players get a good laugh out of this&quot; then &quot;will all of the rules support this action&quot;. For Example i posted a steven universe thread here because while that series isn't always consistent with its mythos and laws of science, when you finally do figure out how everything works, the implications are actually pretty darned funny. It is cool when the technology works in an actual scientific way, but it's way more fun to just enjoy what is already present in the system. Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:39:01-08:00","id":809200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=809019#post809019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, doesn't Core state that the God-Machine is, in fact, <i>not</i> everywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Small pockets of absence are one thing, but having there be an entire continent or so with zero God-Machine would ruin the game because demons would go &quot;fuck it, run for the border&quot;. <br /> <br /> I mean, what possible justification would there be for the G-M to <i>not</i> exist on a global scale, anyway? Angels can fly. It's going to just spread out as far as it will go. Hell, the Storyteller's guide has angels running around in the outer solar system. It's a step or two <i>above</i> &quot;global&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T16:46:10-08:00","id":809207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=809200#post809200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, what possible justification would there be for the G-M to <i>not</i> exist on a global scale, anyway? Angels can fly. It's going to just spread out as far as it will go. Hell, the Storyteller's guide has angels running around in the outer solar system. It's a step or two <i>above</i> &quot;global&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that GM needs infrastructure to do anything + angels are costly to create.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:00:09-08:00","id":809219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808829#post808829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is definitely interesting, and probably the first critique of Demon not being suitable for a &amp;quot;traditional&amp;quot; angels vs. demons game I've read that I can actually understand and agree with. The God-Machine has secret cults of followers, but it's not a genuine religion followed by ordinary people worldwide. Demons are not the amoral opposition to the God-Machine's dogmatic view of morality. I can see how the focus on secrecy and espionage over religion and faith could take the Demon out of Demon the Descent for some people. And unlike the technological aesthetics, that's something you can't easily remove from Descent without changing the game on a fundamental level. And it's something I hadn't even considered because it's such a given to me that any heaven vs. hell conflict in the Chronicles of Darkness would be a secret war between factions that are definitively not the Judeo-Christian versions of heaven and hell. The secrecy is what makes it a CofD game, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I actually like the fact that DtD is like this, as it makes the game playable for me.<br /> <br /> It's also the reason why I consider Inferno to be a better \u201chook\u201d for translating elements of DtF into the ChroD, despite being as just as different from DtF as DtD is: Inferno actually does concern itself with matters of human morality as a central theme. So if that's what you want out of a game about demons \u2014 for them to be involved in the sorts of concerns that religions are actually about \u2014 then Inferno is a much better pick than Descent is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:44:09-08:00","id":809255,"title":"","content":"Except that Inferno doesn't suggest things about the world on the whole in the same way the God-Machine and the Unchained do.<br /> <br /> So, somewhere in-between the two, you've got the classic image. Also Demon the Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T18:48:53-08:00","id":809288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=809219#post809219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also the reason why I consider Inferno to be a better \u201chook\u201d for translating elements of DtF into the ChroD, despite being as just as different from DtF as DtD is: Inferno actually does concern itself with matters of human morality as a central theme. So if that's what you want out of a game about demons \u2014 for them to be involved in the sorts of concerns that religions are actually about \u2014 then Inferno is a much better pick than Descent is.</div> </div> </div> </div> I find it exceedingly interesting that people think that &quot;matters of human morality&quot; has anything to do with Demon the Fallen. It doesn't. DtF was a game about fallen angels who make their way into the world, then start squabbling over who gets to run it. Human morals never once enter into the equation. &quot;Faith&quot; was a thing, but that had more to do with blind belief than to morals. <br /> <br /> I sometimes wonder about Fallen the way some people describe it. I've yet to hear anyone describe anything resembling my experience with that game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T19:36:48-08:00","id":809303,"title":"","content":"No, Faith was a theme in that, and even morality came into it. I mean, come on, as protagonists, you're a millenia old hate spirit who rediscovers love, hope, charity, kindness upon invading another person, and you're opposed by other demons who have existed in the world while having nothing but Torment-colored glasses to see it through and therefore desire nothing good for or upon humanity. If there's not strata of good and evil in there being explored, I'm not sure what's going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T19:45:25-08:00","id":809311,"title":"","content":"I think there's plenty of morality play in Descent. It's just morality play more like Battlestar Galactica, Person of Interest, or (surprise) spy novels than something focused on the cardinal sins. It looks at questions like individual freedom v authority, the needs of the many/few, and making a new life in dangerous and uncertain circumstances with all the complexity that entails.<br /> <br /> Questions not like &quot;which side will you choose, paragon or renegade?&quot; but about choices and priorities and philosophies.<br /> <br /> Semi-related; I'm looking forward to seeing similar technohorror frames approached a different way in Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T20:21:59-08:00","id":809328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=808950#post808950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my favourite Hell, even though I'm a strong advocate of 'If you wanna go big or even kill/fix the God-Machine in your games, do it', is actually an Integrator reuniting with the God-Machine after completing a self-imposed personal mission.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was always one of my favorites, as well. As compelling as a &quot;fixing God&quot; story can be, and as much dramatic potential as there might be in having a PC who is secretly an agent of the Enemy, I always felt that &quot;I'll return to the God-Machine just as soon as I accomplish X&quot; does just as much for answering the question of why an Integrator doesn't just turn herself over to the God-Machine as soon as she Falls. It also makes the Integrator's self-imposed exile so much more personal. Add in the perpetual temptation to move those goal posts, and it's just delicious. It's exactly the sort of character that is catnip to me as a player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T01:56:14-08:00","id":809447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=809207#post809207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that GM needs infrastructure to do anything + angels are costly to create.</div> </div> </div> </div>Countered by the fact that a sufficiently powerful angel can just make Infrastructure out of nothing. Plus the G-M has been around for thousands, if not millions, of years. Even the slowest expansion could swallow up a planet in that time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T02:00:42-08:00","id":809450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=809447#post809447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Countered by the fact that a sufficiently powerful angel can just make Infrastructure out of nothing. Plus the G-M has been around for thousands, if not millions, of years. Even the slowest expansion could swallow up a planet in that time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't mean anything if it isn't maintained. The God Machine's worst enemy is entropy. Doesn't matter if you can do that, you've got to maintain it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T09:40:40-08:00","id":814886,"title":"","content":"You guys know I've been bouncing around this issue. For me, it's just the terminology is easy to mix up. Take &quot;facility&quot; for example. It's not a power word, it's very flat, and easy to overlook. If I'm reading about a facility, how do I differentiate between a normal facility and a different dimension of existence? Give it a capital F?<br /> <br /> That said, maybe we should just take the GM as being the Weaver from cWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:48:24-08:00","id":815051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=814886#post814886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys know I've been bouncing around this issue. For me, it's just the terminology is easy to mix up. Take &quot;facility&quot; for example. It's not a power word, it's very flat, and easy to overlook. If I'm reading about a facility, how do I differentiate between a normal facility and a different dimension of existence? Give it a capital F?<br /> <br /> That said, maybe we should just take the GM as being the Weaver from cWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or not. Because, you know, no.<br /> <br /> Use holy terms if it's hard, but when mostly it comes to tone and your use of words, particularly adjectives and verbs.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, yes, saying it with a capital F does a lot from changing a mere facility to the place where God shows his face, the Facility.<br /> <br /> False comparison, but the word play works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-23-2016, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:52:25-08:00","id":815055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815051#post815051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or not. Because, you know, no.<br /> <br /> Use holy terms if it's hard, but when mostly it comes to tone and your use of words, particularly adjectives and verbs.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, yes, saying it with a capital F does a lot from changing a mere facility to the place where God shows his face, the Facility.<br /> <br /> False comparison, but the word play works.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't make thread crap posts, thanks. Darksider.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 01-23-2016, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T21:51:28-08:00","id":815251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=803393#post803393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's some rationales I've written down. Lemme know if it works, or I'm full of sh*t. ^_^;<br /> <br /> \u2022 Embeds are infallible cosmic truths that demons can enforce onto themselves. Exploits are akin to manipulating the &quot;legalese&quot; of reality, albeit temporary.<br /> \u2022 Terms like propulsion, infrastructure, etc. are simply used to dumb down advanced ideas for &quot;primitive mortals&quot; to comprehend.<br /> \u2022 The God-Machine is not just a collection of machinery, cogs, and gears, but the Spirit of Order itself. Every time a pattern is formed, the God-Machine knows, because they are one in the same.<br /> \u2022 GM is to Demiurge as Promethean Principle is to God(?), perhaps polar opposites, or parent to the other (or both).<br /> \u2022 The demonic form isn't truly made of mundane materials. Rather, a demon is a collection of symbolic truths bound in a quantum state between one or more realities (wow that's a mouthful)--uh, it is a True Name given physical form?<br /> \u2022 The Cipher is a Malapraxis?<br /> <br /> But yeah, I didn't mean Spirit as in Shadow, as more like the GM is sentient symbolism. Software and Hardware are too temporal to equate to something so powerful. The Idea behind the GM, that is what transcends the mundane. It doesn't need circuit boards, not in the conventional sense. Patterns that act akin to circuits, such as leylines touching menhirs to connect with other realms, that is what forms the GM. Transcendental, not material. Ignore the literal idea of a Machine and think bigger, more abstract. It's not a mere robot, but patterns within patterns, made sentient by means unknowable.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I've read through Demon, cover to cover<br /> <br /> and I could have SWORN this is EXACTLY how it works already<br /> <br /> and the cog and gear imagery and the technojargon is just there for human mental convenience<br /> <br /> also Dharmic wheel, Earth-wheel, dreamcatcher, Ouroborous, fairy rings, pi, Ezekiel, the binding of Ixion, kutawa guruma, and many other examples from widely varying cultures really have a thing about wheels and rings and turning of the celestial heavens as a great interlocking mechanism - it could all just be coincidence, sure. But what the hell, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T03:17:45-08:00","id":815338,"title":"","content":"Yeah... the God-Machine as presented in the book is already the cosmic manifestation of the magical symbolism of the 'System', be it human infrastructure or natural laws.<br /> <br /> And as many people said, wheels and gears already feature prominently in real-life lore about the heavens and the workings of the world.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the book also makes clear that Infrastructure, angels, and Demons can all be more 'organic', 'religious', et c.<br /> <br /> Why is everyone <i>still </i>so bothered? I'm starting to get genuinely confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5789-acanthus","name":"acanthus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T03:29:30-08:00","id":815342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>acanthus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815338#post815338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is everyone <i>still </i>so bothered? I'm starting to get genuinely confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point of this thread. I was sincerely confused as to why the issue existed since it seemed easy for me to simply not allow players to take digital form and electric senses when it comes to Demonic Forms. For some, the issue remains because of terminology such as Facility and Propulsion, while for others there are not enough religious aspects, and another individual dislikes the mythological inspiration for the Demons preferring for them to be embodied sins rather than fallen angels of a divine presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:07:38-08:00","id":815386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raygungoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815251#post815251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I've read through Demon, cover to cover<br /> <br /> and I could have SWORN this is EXACTLY how it works already<br /> <br /> and the cog and gear imagery and the technojargon is just there for human mental convenience<br /> <br /> also Dharmic wheel, Earth-wheel, dreamcatcher, Ouroborous, fairy rings, pi, Ezekiel, the binding of Ixion, kutawa guruma, and many other examples from widely varying cultures really have a thing about wheels and rings and turning of the celestial heavens as a great interlocking mechanism - it could all just be coincidence, sure. But what the hell, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>My, such passion! I am behooved to ask what makes you think specifically <i><b>wheels</b></i> are the problem? Be it stone or wood or metal, be it cog or pipe or circuit board, the problem is not there. The difficulty in which we find ourselves in is on how to make modest the use of cyberpunk material. From this, all demons stem from, as the subtitle of Techgnostic Espionage implies.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, that was my way of explaining the setting to people. Thanks for giving me the benefit of the doubt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 01-24-2016, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:38:00-08:00","id":815404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>acanthus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815338#post815338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is everyone <i>still </i>so bothered? I'm starting to get genuinely confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm not bothered personally since I genuinely quite like the way Demon is presented with the techgnostic elements. However perhaps I can explain why others do not.<br /> <br /> When it comes to narrative themes there's a big difference between science, magic and religion. Each of these three are used in different ways when you're telling stories. I'll boil it down to just one small aspect because I can't possibly cover everything. It's much more than just this one aspect that I'm referring to though.<br /> <br /> The scientist does what works, even if it doesn't make sense, because it gives them results.<br /> The mage does what should work by symbolic logic as a deliberate attempt to gain results.<br /> The priest does what they're supposed to because it's right, regardless of results.<br /> <br /> Demon, quite deliberately in my opinion, attempts to use all three in describing the God Machine. However, when it comes to how the God Machine works we almost always only see it done through a process that's scientific, magical or a combination of both. It builds infrastructure to achieve results, not because it's right that it should. The divine and religious aspects of the God Machine are mostly only used for their grandeur rather than being frequently invoked in the setting.<br /> <br /> It's not just this process. The most common aspects of at least Abrahamic religions, faith, identity, morality, community, dogma and personal relationships with the divine are either only used in twisted forms for small cults or excluded altogether. The G-M is only a god in power and terror but in all other ways it doesn't really reflect that mode of storytelling associated with religion. Instead it's a form of cosmic horror like H.P. Lovecraft's Cthulu mythos.<br /> <br /> I'm perfectly happy with this and it's the game that I want to play. However for people who were looking for something a little more Paradise Lost, they may find a lot of clashes with that in far more deep thematic issues rather than a surface aesthetic of cogs and gears. Given that Demon: The Fallen was from more so this perspective and Inferno... well, was somewhere in the middle, it's not surprising that some people expected to find it here in Demon: The Descent.<br /> <br /> I do think it's possible for a storyteller to re-emphasize these aspects and shift Demon back to include some religious aspects to the G-M, but it's a tricky task and I think many people troubled thematically by Demon don't really recognize that this may be the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T07:31:27-08:00","id":815432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815404#post815404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I'm not bothered personally since I genuinely quite like the way Demon is presented with the techgnostic elements. However perhaps I can explain why others do not.<br /> <br /> When it comes to narrative themes there's a big difference between science, magic and religion. Each of these three are used in different ways when you're telling stories. I'll boil it down to just one small aspect because I can't possibly cover everything. It's much more than just this one aspect that I'm referring to though.<br /> <br /> The scientist does what works, even if it doesn't make sense, because it gives them results.<br /> The mage does what should work by symbolic logic as a deliberate attempt to gain results.<br /> The priest does what they're supposed to because it's right, regardless of results.<br /> <br /> Demon, quite deliberately in my opinion, attempts to use all three in describing the God Machine. However, when it comes to how the God Machine works we almost always only see it done through a process that's scientific, magical or a combination of both. It builds infrastructure to achieve results, not because it's right that it should. The divine and religious aspects of the God Machine are mostly only used for their grandeur rather than being frequently invoked in the setting.<br /> <br /> It's not just this process. The most common aspects of at least Abrahamic religions, faith, identity, morality, community, dogma and personal relationships with the divine are either only used in twisted forms for small cults or excluded altogether. The G-M is only a god in power and terror but in all other ways it doesn't really reflect that mode of storytelling associated with religion. Instead it's a form of cosmic horror like H.P. Lovecraft's Cthulu mythos.<br /> <br /> I'm perfectly happy with this and it's the game that I want to play. However for people who were looking for something a little more Paradise Lost, they may find a lot of clashes with that in far more deep thematic issues rather than a surface aesthetic of cogs and gears. Given that Demon: The Fallen was from more so this perspective and Inferno... well, was somewhere in the middle, it's not surprising that some people expected to find it here in Demon: The Descent.<br /> <br /> I do think it's possible for a storyteller to re-emphasize these aspects and shift Demon back to include some religious aspects to the G-M, but it's a tricky task and I think many people troubled thematically by Demon don't really recognize that this may be the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:30:53-08:00","id":815585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815386#post815386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the use of cyberpunk material</div> </div> </div> </div>Identify sans-scareword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T14:14:06-08:00","id":815681,"title":"","content":"I think part of the reason faith and dogma are less used in Demon is because your sorta a character who has lost their faith. The faith aspect in demon ties in two main ways, the integrator agenda and the cults being manipulated.<br /> <br /> Also is it weird I sorta think that if a divinity existed it's angels and demons wouldn't really be fighting over religious things because... well they know what's true and what isn't and for them it's just War rather than a religious war? I mean.... you don't Need faith in a deity when you used to be one of it's personal servants and physically interact with it elements of it on a daily basis.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T14:18:40-08:00","id":815683,"title":"","content":"It may be worth noting that the core book is a lot about fallen angels and not a lot about God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T14:20:46-08:00","id":815684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815681#post815681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the reason faith and dogma are less used in Demon is because your sorta a character who has lost their faith. The faith aspect in demon ties in two main ways, the integrator agenda and the cults being manipulated.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, it sometimes gets lost that Integrators might be <i>right</i>. Their beliefs and goals go against the accepted standards among their peers, but this is often true of people with great insight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T14:37:14-08:00","id":815693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815684#post815684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the way, it sometimes gets lost that Integrators might be <i>right</i>. Their beliefs and goals go against the accepted standards among their peers, but this is often true of people with great insight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've actually always liked that there are good aspects to the God-Machine so that while there might be issues, you can never be sure and go &quot;GM is evil&quot; because it might just be working in ways you don't understand to help people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T15:39:41-08:00","id":815728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815693#post815693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I've actually always liked that there are good aspects to the God-Machine so that while there might be issues, you can never be sure and go &quot;GM is evil&quot; because it might just be working in ways you don't understand to help people.</div> </div> </div> </div>The things in the real world that the God-Machine's methods most resemble, like social structures and political systems, are rarely unalloyed good or evil. The God-Machine is the system we're born into without our consent, but sometimes that system supports us.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">(EDIT: They're also rarely systems of narrow, single purpose.)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 01-24-2016, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T17:14:14-08:00","id":815770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815681#post815681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the reason faith and dogma are less used in Demon is because your sorta a character who has lost their faith. The faith aspect in demon ties in two main ways, the integrator agenda and the cults being manipulated.<br /> <br /> Also is it weird I sorta think that if a divinity existed it's angels and demons wouldn't really be fighting over religious things because... well they know what's true and what isn't and for them it's just War rather than a religious war? I mean.... you don't Need faith in a deity when you used to be one of it's personal servants and physically interact with it elements of it on a daily basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying it doesn't make sense. I'm saying why it was a thematic choice which doesn't resonate with every group of readers. This certainly isn't a criticism of Demon, I love the choices that they made with it. I want a game of techgnostic espionage against a backdrop of cosmic horror. It's just not what everyone's looking for and because it's a very deep and substantial game, superficial alterations to the aesthetics isn't enough to really change that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T17:46:32-08:00","id":815787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815770#post815770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not saying it doesn't make sense. I'm saying why it was a thematic choice which doesn't resonate with every group of readers. This certainly isn't a criticism of Demon, I love the choices that they made with it. I want a game of techgnostic espionage against a backdrop of cosmic horror. It's just not what everyone's looking for and because it's a very deep and substantial game, superficial alterations to the aesthetics isn't enough to really change that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mainly just stating that I sincerely don't understand how it being more religious would work in a game of demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T02:09:25-08:00","id":815964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons#post802411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been said by a few people that they dislike the technological nature of Demons and the God-Machine (though I personally disagree, liking how well it fits with Ezekiel). Now, I understand the preference of Demons should be more mystical rather than bio-mechanical beings, as it is a valid preference. But what I don't understand is why the technological nature is hard to remove?<br /> <br /> Can the issue be fixed in your personal games by simply restricting access to Demonic Form abilities that are technological? If not, what other things conflict with altering the to your desire? As far as I'm aware, everything else in the game is fitting for more generalized interpretations of demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your first idea is there in your post.<br /> <br /> Ezekiel 1:4-9<br /> <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-4.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>4</b></a>I looked, and I saw a windstorm coming out of the north--an immense cloud with flashing lightning and surrounded by brilliant light. The center of the fire looked like glowing metal, <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-5.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>5</b></a>and in the fire was what looked like four living creatures. In appearance their form was human, <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-6.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>6</b></a>but each of them had four faces and four wings. <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-7.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>7</b></a>Their legs were straight; their feet were like those of a calf and gleamed like burnished bronze. <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-8.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>8</b></a>Under their wings on their four sides they had human hands. All four of them had faces and wings, <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-9.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>9</b></a>and the wings of one touched the wings of another. Each one went straight ahead; they did not turn as they moved.<br /> <br /> Simply paint the technologies of the God-Machine as arcane in design. Here are some examples off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Electrical Sight doesn't need to change at all, but perhaps rename it to: I See The Light or something flavourful like that. Angels, and demons, are luminous beings after all.<br /> <br /> Rivet-Arm allows you to get creative. You could go for something such as a cross-bow built into angelic armour or something more weird and unreal like an arm that shoots crucifix nails.<br /> <br /> Plasma Drive becomes Messenger's Motion. Then illustrate it's appearance as a glowing radiance flows from the Demon's skin, shining like the sun caught beneath the flesh.<br /> <br /> Tether becomes Serpent's Tail. Then illustrate it as a fiery or fleshy serpentine tail. Maybe add a thorn, spine, spade or stinger for effect at player discretion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I disagree with the assertion that Demon: the Descent lacks any distinct religious undertones. I think that it has them in spades. The God-Machine's primary operations are supported by cults; it manipulates and utilises belief systems that exist independent of it or creates new belief systems whole-sale with the deployment of an angel. A Demon often has to infiltrate these cults, witness the faults and fallacies that faith - an otherwise altruistic trait - can create when bent to certain extremes. Then a Demon, as a traitor and a turn-coat to God-Machine and Its design, has to decide against the workings of God-Machine on a personal, moral level and decide on a per event basis with no knowledge of the possible consequences. This is muddied even further by the fact, as Rose said, the Integrators might be <i>right.</i> God-Machine might be a benevolent being purely working on a scale, as God Himself, and therefore beyond our limited perception. The moral ambiguity of spy play and a need to survive all further feed into a heavily moralistic game. Should you do something because it's right? What is right? If I go back in time and kill a mass-murderer like Adolf Hitler, have I done the universe good by saving his millions of victims or have I created millions more through a chain-reaction which results in the Soviet Union becoming a much more economically powerful and oppressive regime? A Demon has to wrestle with these questions. Is 'good' good because it feels good? If so, why does 'evil' feel 'good'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 01-25-2016, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T03:24:19-08:00","id":815992,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/815989-story-as-rain-falls-the-flame\">This story</a> I wrote for a character I want to play details almost literally removing the gears. I wanted something still befitting the game, but with a slightly more traditional look and trappings. So I created it. The game works just even if you do stuff like that. After all, this is a game in which truths are constantly hidden; in machines, in mysteries, in minds, in madness. Metaphor, veiled truths, webs of lies, all of these things come together to create the game's imagery. A battle between angels and demons might be a clash of celestial warriors and hideous beasts, with light and hellfire filling the sky. It might be a gun battle between mafiosos clad in expensive suits and bio-mechanical vultures with opera masks covering their bellies. Couching these conflicts within religious imagery is probably a favored tactic for both the God-Machine and the Unchained. It lets them hide more easily even as they wage shadow-war, and it lets them turn mortals to their side more easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T03:27:45-08:00","id":815995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815964#post815964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ezekiel 1:4-9<br /> <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-4.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>4</b></a>I looked, and I saw a windstorm coming out of the north--an immense cloud with flashing lightning and surrounded by brilliant light. The center of the fire looked like glowing metal, <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-5.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>5</b></a>and in the fire was what looked like four living creatures. In appearance their form was human, <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-6.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>6</b></a>but each of them had four faces and four wings. <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-7.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>7</b></a>Their legs were straight; their feet were like those of a calf and gleamed like burnished bronze. <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-8.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>8</b></a>Under their wings on their four sides they had human hands. All four of them had faces and wings, <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/ezekiel/1-9.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><b>9</b></a>and the wings of one touched the wings of another. Each one went straight ahead; they did not turn as they moved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I know. That's why I didn't understand the issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tether becomes Serpent's Tail. Then illustrate it as a fiery or fleshy serpentine tail. Maybe add a thorn, spine, spade or stinger for effect at player discretion. </div> </div> </div>Heh, I was actually making a Wheel the other day with Tether, was spinnerettes because it's form was a giant demonic spider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I disagree with the assertion that Demon: the Descent lacks any distinct religious undertones. \u200b I think that it has them in spades. </div> </div> </div>I agree. But it's simply that some people think the religious tones are minimal in the areas such as faith and that it doesn't Feel like a religious conflict. Though I have already said my feelings on those two issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T03:43:49-08:00","id":815998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815787#post815787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was mainly just stating that I sincerely don't understand how it being more religious would work in a game of demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd give a Fallen a read then. The central question isn't faith in the existence of God, it's faith in the providence of God. Remember most relgious people don't just believe in a deity, they believe that that deity has some kind of benevolent plan. Also, in Fallen, the angels never fully understand God (and really they can't). God gives the angels apparently contradictory orders, and not really understanding the consequences, they disobey it.<br /> <br /> There's also the secondary faith that the demons have in Lucifer their leader. He's described in terms of a sort of demonic Jesus, the great leader who will return and free us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T04:07:34-08:00","id":816005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=815998#post815998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd give a Fallen a read then. The central question isn't faith in the existence of God, it's faith in the providence of God. Remember most relgious people don't just believe in a deity, they believe that that deity has some kind of benevolent plan. Also, in Fallen, the angels never fully understand God (and really they can't). God gives the angels apparently contradictory orders, and not really understanding the consequences, they disobey it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it interesting that you say this since that is the exact same as in Descent thus again, I'm wondering &quot;<i>how it being more religious would work in a game of demons.&quot;</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T04:22:24-08:00","id":816010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816005#post816005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that you say this since that is the exact same as in Descent thus again, I'm wondering &quot;<i>how it being more religious would work in a game of demons.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Which bit? I made two different statements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T04:34:54-08:00","id":816015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816010#post816010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which bit? I made two different statements.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first bit, I don't really understand how the lucifer bit ties into religious style faith and think I should probably read information on that situation before I comment on something I am ignorant on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T04:59:46-08:00","id":816023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816015#post816015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first bit, I don't really understand how the lucifer bit ties into religious style faith and think I should probably read information on that situation before I comment on something I am ignorant on.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first bit that's in the second paragraph?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T05:22:56-08:00","id":816028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816023#post816023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first bit that's in the second paragraph?</div> </div> </div> </div>My initial reply was to the first thing. Me mentioning the second paragraph in the second reply was giving my reason on why I did not comment on the second paragraph, since I am ignorant in regard to Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T06:22:14-08:00","id":816049,"title":"","content":"I actually made three statements and you quoted two of them, so I wanted to know which you were referring to so as to not to misunderstand you.<br /> <br /> But in the interests of brevity:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816005#post816005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that you say this since that is the exact same as in Descent thus again, I'm wondering &quot;<i>how it being more religious would work in a game of demons.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Context. Broadly speaking the Fallen fell because they wanted to help humanity, but in the process they pretty much ruined both humanity and the universe. Therefore the doubt in their decision to defy God is given a great deal more weight than in Descent where most Demons fall in pretty small ways. The Unchained may feel bad, but it's generally just not that important in the grand scheme of things. Further, as a result it's quite possible for them to feel totally unrepentant in their choice and never really doubt themselves. That's clearly not true of the Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:22:09-08:00","id":816224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816049#post816049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually made three statements and you quoted two of them, so I wanted to know which you were referring to so as to not to misunderstand you.<br /> <br /> But in the interests of brevity:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Context. Broadly speaking the Fallen fell because they wanted to help humanity, but in the process they pretty much ruined both humanity and the universe. Therefore the doubt in their decision to defy God is given a great deal more weight than in Descent where most Demons fall in pretty small ways. The Unchained may feel bad, but it's generally just not that important in the grand scheme of things. Further, as a result it's quite possible for them to feel totally unrepentant in their choice and never really doubt themselves. That's clearly not true of the Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically, you can have the same reasons and outlook in Fallen, they are just given less emphasis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:42:13-08:00","id":816304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816049#post816049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually made three statements and you quoted two of them, so I wanted to know which you were referring to so as to not to misunderstand you.<br /> <br /> But in the interests of brevity:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Context. Broadly speaking the Fallen fell because they wanted to help humanity, but in the process they pretty much ruined both humanity and the universe. Therefore the doubt in their decision to defy God is given a great deal more weight than in Descent where most Demons fall in pretty small ways. The Unchained may feel bad, but it's generally just not that important in the grand scheme of things. Further, as a result it's quite possible for them to feel totally unrepentant in their choice and never really doubt themselves. That's clearly not true of the Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fallen has three factions that clearly aren't repentent-the Luciferans, the Faustians, and the Ravagers. That's the majority of factions.<br /> <br /> As a contrasting comparison(It is ultimately a comparison), Descent's central theme of faith is different from Fallen's faith(really, it's a matter of angles, because it ends up talking about a lot of the same ideas), but that idea of faith deals with the trust reading of the word. Doubt, by necessity, is the main enemy of the game, and that extends to the individual level. Everything you are is more or less because of the God-Machine. How right can you be in contrast to the Machine? Integrators may openly suggest it, but every demon, when faced with the world of the Machine, vast and all-knowing and invisible, is going to ask themselves-<br /> <br /> <i>Was I wrong to turn from You?</i><br /> <br /> In Descent and Fallen, you have to ask that question every night. The contexts are different, but the faith is always challenged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:47:36-08:00","id":816359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816304#post816304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fallen has three factions that clearly aren't repentent-the Luciferans, the Faustians, and the Ravagers. That's the majority of factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good job I didn't say repentent then. My point is that doubt in their choice is inherent in the setting because of the sheer amunt of suffering and that the demons have pretty uniformly failed in their objectives. That doesn't stop them reaffirming their beliefs, but that doubt is pretty omnipresent.<br /> <br /> Also, the Raveners in particular are actually entirely about doubt. Theyre unrepentent, but they've given up entirely on their objectives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everything you are is more or less because of the God-Machine. How right can you be in contrast to the Machine? Integrators may openly suggest it, but every demon, when faced with the world of the Machine, vast and all-knowing and invisible, is going to ask themselves-<br /> <i>Was I wrong to turn from You?</i> </div> </div> </div>I kinda see where you're coming from with this. However, I don't think it has nearly have the same weight. Firstly, it's not much of a decision. Demons fall for all kinds of reasons including failure to carry out orders and becuase orders are mutually contradictory; those don't have much choice in the matter. Secondly, that's a largely empty statement. The Fallen's choice had actual longterm negative consequences, for the Unchained that's generally not true or at least, it's completely uncertain, made additionally problematic by the fact that the GM doesn't really claim any moral authority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:30:02-08:00","id":816388,"title":"","content":"I can't speak for others, but the mechanical aspect of Demon and the God-Machine are basically what breaks the game for me. I know many people said &quot;just don't use this aesthetic then&quot; but it just doesn't work for me no matter what, mostly because reading a 400 pages book while having to para-read everything is not my way to go.<br /> <br /> A few reasons why I don't like the aesthetic:<ul><li>Machines suddenly gain emotions due to failures - my toaster does not become a sentient being simply because I press all buttons while plugging him on two different circuits</li> <li>A giant machine from the future hacked reality and ingrained itself in every atoms - I thought this was the ChroD, where things are occult, not technologic. Alien: The Abduction is not a thing because Sci-Fi is not the way the devs want to go</li> <li>The Promethean Fallacy Argument - No matter what I do, the Machine will know and send angels at me. I can't get a rest, ever. Also, said Angels can hack into every person I trust and commit suicide in front of me repeatedly and there's nothing I can do to stop it.</li> <li>The weird quantum explanation for demons.</li> <li>No matter how many times the book tells me about the emotions and feelings of a demon, I can't shake off the fact that they are machines and thus don't feel anything.</li> <li>Having a chainsaw as an arm and a pair of jetpack-wings is cool until you remember that demons were present in constantinople</li> <li>Demons greatest asset is human lives patchworked together. I've seen arguments that the Machine cannot rewire your brain, but Covers can basically tell reality that you've always been this person's father. Instant, perfect, timeless memory and reality manipulation.</li> </ul>I <i>know</i> these are not true. Demons <i>have</i> emotions, the GM is not a litteral machine, you can catch a break, demon-form is malleable, etc... but to me it feels the same as saying Mages are not people able to enact their will on the world but programmers knowing the code to the world, or Werewolf being a Transformer game. Mechanics can be fine, themes can be fine, Aesthetic is important and conveys information and mood and preconceived ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T17:02:11-08:00","id":816510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816388#post816388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Machines suddenly gain emotions due to failures - my toaster does not become a sentient being simply because I press all buttons while plugging him on two different circuits</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is grossly (and unfairly) reductionist on the concept of emergent intelligence. Angels as presented in DtD are complex, sapient, reasoning beings capable of both learning and rewriting what they know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T17:18:25-08:00","id":816518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816388#post816388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak for others, but the mechanical aspect of Demon and the God-Machine are basically what breaks the game for me. I know many people said &quot;just don't use this aesthetic then&quot; but it just doesn't work for me no matter what, mostly because reading a 400 pages book while having to para-read everything is not my way to go.<br /> <br /> A few reasons why I don't like the aesthetic:[LIST][*]Machines suddenly gain emotions due to failures - my toaster does not become a sentient being simply because I press all buttons while plugging him on two different circuits</div> </div> </div> </div>They get emotions because all their spiritual ephemeral being is forced into co-existance with a human body, gaining a human mind. It's a spiritual being that has been cast out, and forced to possess the body (including brain) of the human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]A giant machine from the future hacked reality and ingrained itself in every atoms - I thought this was the ChroD, where things are occult, not technologic. Alien: The Abduction is not a thing because Sci-Fi is not the way the devs want to go </div> </div> </div>Just because it is mechanical does not mean it's not occult. Have you read how infrastructure works, it's things like &quot;The omnipresent divinity needs to alter how time works in a city, and to do so four people have to die within 100 feet of a clocktower within a spanse of a single minute. So angels and cults are formed so that the clocktowers are built and obscured, and then ritual sacrifices occur so that all the current things are in place for the occult energies to accomplish the time manipulation.&quot; The godmachine, may be a machine, but basically all of it's actions are done via occult methods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]The Promethean Fallacy Argument - No matter what I do, the Machine will know and send angels at me. I can't get a rest, ever. Also, said Angels can hack into every person I trust and commit suicide in front of me repeatedly and there's nothing I can do to stop it. </div> </div> </div>That's not true at all... I've found it's actually rather easy to stay off the radar, the trouble is that if you are interfering with the God's angels or infrastructure because you want to stop it from manipulating humanity or you start trying to jailbreak reality with exploits, then the god-machine might notice you. It's not &quot;No matter what the God-Machine will find me.&quot; it's &quot;Can I risk taking this mission if it means I might get compromised?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]No matter how many times the book tells me about the emotions and feelings of a demon, I can't shake off the fact that they are machines and thus don't feel anything. </div> </div> </div>Considering there are demons with forms made of fire. Demons can be 100% organic without issue. Demons can be big red guys with horns and a devil's tail. Demons can be massive spiders (my current character). Demons can be stony gargoyles. Demons are not machines, they Were machines. But now they are more than just a program of the machine. They once were just a program in reality making sure the system works, that gravity attracts, that rain falls, that snowflakes don't all arrange themselves exactly the same for every instance. But now, you strayed from Gods orders and you fell... Unchained from the system and now merged with humanity, you are no longer just a program or a machine. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Having a chainsaw as an arm and a pair of jetpack-wings is cool until you remember that demons were present in constantinople </div> </div> </div>Notice that every single demonic form ability has two things listed for it's appearance, how it could look mechanically, and how it could look organically. So... there is no reason why that's required. Also.... why not have superior technology in olden times. Do you not think such a being would look eldritch and demonic if it were a being in ancient times with flesh of bone that reflects like water and eyes of lightning. Or something like... a being made of wheels within wheels... which is an actual biblical thing. Back in olden times, technological demons would appear Less Technological, because such a thing is truly beyond them. They do not see a demon with a jetpack, they see a demon who ascends upon a pillar of flame and smoke. They do not see a demon with a chainsaw, they see a demon with thorns of bone erupted from their arms that scream and eviscerate in a frenzy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Demons greatest asset is human lives patchworked together. I've seen arguments that the Machine cannot rewire your brain, but Covers can basically tell reality that you've always been this person's father. Instant, perfect, timeless memory and reality manipulation. </div> </div> </div>The Machine can rewire your brain.... many demons are fearful of being caught because they know they'll be converted back into angels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages are not people able to enact their will on the world but programmers knowing the code to the world </div> </div> </div>You know that it actually is Both right? There's a reason why they have mage-sight and that matrix is a good inspiration for playing Mage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T19:08:31-08:00","id":816580,"title":"","content":"Loyal angels have emotions, or at least most of them do. They just haven't chosen to let those emotions lead them astray. Likewise, they're fully thinking beings, capable of independent thought and action but not having yet chosen it. &quot;Malfunction&quot; is the way the God-Machine probably thinks of angels going rogue, so we use it a bit, but the idea isn't that machines become sapient because they break. It's that to an entity so large it can only be called God, anything that defies its will must be failing. Much the same as Adam and Eve committed &quot;original sin,&quot; as defined by a God who couldn't conceive of failure to obey as anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T21:07:03-08:00","id":816646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816580#post816580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loyal angels have emotions, or at least most of them do. They just haven't chosen to let those emotions lead them astray. Likewise, they're fully thinking beings, capable of independent thought and action but not having yet chosen it. &quot;Malfunction&quot; is the way the God-Machine probably thinks of angels going rogue, so we use it a bit, but the idea isn't that machines become sapient because they break. It's that to an entity so large it can only be called God, anything that defies its will must be failing. Much the same as Adam and Eve committed &quot;original sin,&quot; as defined by a God who couldn't conceive of failure to obey as anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building on this, it's worth restating that the God-Machine chiefly looks at entities as a collection of roles and resources \u2014 the Machine doesn't especially care that Ms. Conduct found the prospect of turning a family of four into an undying Essence-generator aesthetically repugnant, but it does care that it lost a Psychopomp, a key aetheric flywheel in the occult matrix meant to screen the city's quietest residential district from ghostly incursion, and the esoteric equivalent of US$2.4B, among other practical considerations.<br /> <br /> From this perspective, that Adriel did not make good on the investment of resources its summoning necessitated can only be termed an error in the angel itself. This perspective is not one that looks at demons as people, because it is not one that looks at <i>people</i> as people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T05:26:26-08:00","id":816798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/802411-removing-the-gears-in-demons?p=816518#post816518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do not see a demon with a jetpack, they see a demon who ascends upon a pillar of flame and smoke. They do not see a demon with a chainsaw, they see a demon with thorns of bone erupted from their arms that scream and eviscerate in a frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the ones that have <i>swords coming out of their mouths</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:14:31-08:00","id":816853,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all your answers but as I said, I know most of these things. My point was that their presentation <i>as machines, </i>even with feelings and complex interactions with humanity, is what makes Demon a no-sell to me. Not because the themes or concepts or mechanics are not interesting, not because these can't be translated to a more fire &amp; brimstone demon, simply because in order for me to <i>want</i> to do all this reading and converting, I need to be hooked and interested in the game, and the whole &quot;cogs within cogs within an occult furnace using mortal souls as fuel in order to power God's equivalent of a lightbulb&quot; does not hook or interest me at all. And I'm certain I'm not the only one.<br /> <br /> One of the main question of this thread was: &quot;Why can't people see that there's more to the game than the technological aspect&quot;.<br /> <br /> My answer to that is: &quot;Because we need to be hooked to the reading in order to appreciate all these nuances, and the whole Matrix thing rebukes us rather than hooking us in.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because of course the game is more than syringe-fingered, humanoid-shaped machines brainwashing humanity. Of course the game has all the themes of divinity and freedom and fate and faith. Of course the aesthetics can be changed. Of course it's occult. Of course it suits some readings of Ezekiel.<br /> <br /> I just can't read more than a few pages without going &quot;Oh right. It's the Matrix and we're fucked. Why am I reading this?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:44:34-08:00","id":816868,"title":"","content":"I used to be the same way, but it clicked that it's still a game about <i>fallen angels</i><i> as demons</i>. Aren't Biblical angels essentially thoughtless automatons in service of a greater picture?<br /> <br /> But anyway. Not everyone has to like every game. For example, while they were my first two big hooks into the <b>CofD</b>, the more I learn about the other game lines the less interest I have in <b>Hunter</b> and <b>Changeling</b>. The latter even more so now that some of 2e has been previewed.<br /> <br /> I was fortunate in the last regard, though, as I realized <b>Changeling the Dreaming</b>is what I actually want out of a WoD/CofD faerie game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T07:53:39-08:00","id":816880,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;thoughtless automatons&quot; is perhaps a little closer to <i>Qu'ranic</i> angels, but yeah, there's still a definite precedent for DtD angels being precisely what the Abrahamic texts describe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T09:18:28-08:00","id":816933,"title":"","content":"As I see it, the \u201ctechno-\u201d bit is to DtD as spirits and animism are to WtF. They're what make <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OurAngelsAreDifferent\" target=\"_blank\">the GM's Angels so different</a>. <br /> <br /> BTW: have I mentioned that I <i>like</i> the fact that the Unchained aren't in rebellion against a benevolent, all-powerful God? It's what makes them playable for me. If the God-Machine <i>could</i> be mistaken for the biblical God, I'd swear off the game. For me, the fact that it's a game about espionage rather than religious beliefs is a <i>feature</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T15:36:05-08:00","id":817211,"title":"","content":"Fortunately for everyone turned off by technognostic demons, the Demon the Descent Kickstarter and further offerings from the game are very clear about what the game is about and it isn't exactly something anyone should feel ambushed by. And the more traditional <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/636/Demon-The-Fallen?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Demon the Fallen</a> can be purchased on DriveThruRPG with the same ease as Descent, as well as presumably hundreds of other demon games that are likely to satisfy their specific interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:46:49-08:00","id":818570,"title":"","content":"'kay, I've calmed down a bit. Bi-polar depression's a bitch. Took time to read deeper into the material. Looks mostly like my problem was wordplay. Don't feel like going through the entire lexicon to just reflavor the text, but that's my own problem. Maybe they'll have some suggestions when Dark Eras comes around. Hell, maybe Inferno demons are represented in Beast: the Primordial, to balance out the mechanized Order of the GM. Otherwise, the system is strong enough that nit-picking is all that's left to criticize, from a gamer-perspective.<br /> <br /> I have a lot to think about...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}